Since I'm on this week (thanks to the swap with Dev) and have opinions at 3am:

1. Four people in a weekly rotation means everyone is on call one week in four, plus every swap moves it around. That was fine at 6 customers. At 11 plants with overnight shifts it's a lot.
2. Handoff is Monday 9am, which is exactly when Monday's ingest spike lands. The person coming on inherits the spike cold, with no context.
3. Proposal: (a) move handoff to Monday 10am, after the spike, (b) some kind of rule about Friday deploys, (c) longer term, a fifth person.

Not urgent. Just don't want to be the only one saying it.

